    "chunk_text": "8. (1) The Chairman of the Authority shall, if present preside at everymeeting of the Authority. In the absence of the Chairman from any suchmeeting, one of the full-time members present shall preside, and in the absenceof, the Chairman and all the full-time members from any meeting of theAuthority, the members present at such meeting shall elect one of the memberspresent, to preside at such meeting.\n\n(2) The quorum for any meeting of the Authority shall be fourmembers.\n\n(4) Subject to the provisions of this paragraph and any regulation madeunder section 71 the Authority may regulate the procedure in regard to itsmeetings and the transaction of business at such meetings.\n\n9. No act, decision or proceeding of the Authority shall be deemed invalidby reason only of the existence of a vacancy among its members or anydefect in the appointment of any member thereof.\n\n10. (1) The seal of the Authority shall be in the custody of theChairman.\n\n(2) The application of the seal of the Authority shall be authenticated bythe signature of the Chairman or some other member of the Authorityauthorised to authenticate the application of such seal.\n\nTermination ofappointment ofChairman.\n\nMeetings of theAuthority.\n\nSeal of theAuthority.\n\nProceedings act ordecision not todeemed invalid byreason of anydefect in theappointment.\n\nConsumer Affairs Authority Act, No.9 of 200351\n\nDisclosure ofinterest bymembers.\n\n11. A member of the Authority who is directly or indirectly interestedin any matter which forms the subject matter of any proceeding of theAuthority or of any decision proposed to be made by the Authority, shalldisclose the nature of his interest at a meeting of the Authority and suchmember shall not take part in any proceeding or decision in respect of suchmatter.\n\n52Consumer Affairs Authority Act, No.9 of 2003"
